[
 {
  "piece": "MANNING",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2404.11794/2404.11794v2.pdf",
  "empreinte": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "page": 1,
  "citation": "We present an approach for automatically generating and testing, in silico, social scientific hypotheses.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   1
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "MANNING",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2404.11794/2404.11794v2.pdf",
  "empreinte": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "page": 1,
  "citation": "In each case, causal relationships are both proposed and tested by the system, finding evidence for some and not others.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   1
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "MANNING",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2404.11794/2404.11794v2.pdf",
  "empreinte": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "page": 1,
  "citation": "We provide evidence that the insights from these simulations of social interactions are not available to the LLM purely through direct elicitation.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   1
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "MANNING",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2404.11794/2404.11794v2.pdf",
  "empreinte": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "page": 1,
  "citation": "Author’s contact information, code, and data are currently or will be available at http://www.benjaminmanning.io/.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   1
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "MANNING",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2404.11794/2404.11794v2.pdf",
  "empreinte": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "page": 2,
  "citation": "We evaluate the approach by comparing results to a setting where the real-world predictions are well known and test to see if an LLM can be used to generate information that it cannot access through direct elicitation.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   2
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "MANNING",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2404.11794/2404.11794v2.pdf",
  "empreinte": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "page": 2,
  "citation": "algorithms to find anomalies in formal theories (Mullainathan and Rambachan, 2023)",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   2
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "MANNING",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2404.11794/2404.11794v2.pdf",
  "empreinte": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "page": 2,
  "citation": "generative adversarial networks to formulate new hypotheses (Ludwig and Mullainathan, 2023)",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   2
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "MANNING",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2404.11794/2404.11794v2.pdf",
  "empreinte": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "page": 3,
  "citation": "For (3) and (4), we demonstrate the system’s ability to accommodate human input at any point by selecting the hypotheses ourselves and editing some of the agents",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   3
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "MANNING",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2404.11794/2404.11794v2.pdf",
  "empreinte": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "page": 3,
  "citation": "Though yet to be optimized for novelty, the system formulates and tests multiple falsifiable hypotheses—from which it generates several findings.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   3
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "MANNING",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2404.11794/2404.11794v2.pdf",
  "empreinte": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "page": 3,
  "citation": "None of the findings from the system’s experiments are “counterintuitive,” but it is important to emphasize they were the result of empiricism, not just model introspection.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   3
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "MANNING",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2404.11794/2404.11794v2.pdf",
  "empreinte": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "page": 3,
  "citation": "These simulation results closely match the theory (Maskin and Riley, 1985) and what has been observed empirically (Athey et al., 2011).",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   3
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "MANNING",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2404.11794/2404.11794v2.pdf",
  "empreinte": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "page": 3,
  "citation": "However, the judge’s case count before the hearing—which was hypothesized to matter—did not affect the final bail amount.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   3
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "MANNING",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2404.11794/2404.11794v2.pdf",
  "empreinte": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "page": 4,
  "citation": "To test this idea, we describe the experiments that will be simulated and ask the LLM to predict the results—both the path estimates and point predictions.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   4
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "MANNING",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2404.11794/2404.11794v2.pdf",
  "empreinte": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "page": 7,
  "citation": "The first step is to generate hypotheses as SCMs based on the social scenario, the scenario being the only necessary input to the system.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   7
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "MANNING",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2404.11794/2404.11794v2.pdf",
  "empreinte": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "page": 7,
  "citation": "Researchers can edit the system’s decisions at any step in the process.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   7
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "MANNING",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2404.11794/2404.11794v2.pdf",
  "empreinte": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "page": 8,
  "citation": "LLM for the relevant agents and then interesting outcomes, their potential causes, and methods to operationalize and measure both.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   8
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "MANNING",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2404.11794/2404.11794v2.pdf",
  "empreinte": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "page": 9,
  "citation": "After each agent speaks in a simulation, an external LLM is prompted with the transcript of the conversation and asked if the conversation should continue.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   9
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "MANNING",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2404.11794/2404.11794v2.pdf",
  "empreinte": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "page": 10,
  "citation": "Note that an SCM specifies, ex-ante, the exact statistical analyses to be conducted after the experiment—akin to a pre-analysis plan. This step of the system’s process is, therefore, mechanical.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   10
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "MANNING",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2404.11794/2404.11794v2.pdf",
  "empreinte": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "page": 10,
  "citation": "Although we have not automated the transition from one experiment to the next, the system can generate new causal variables, induce variations, and run another experiment based on the results of the first.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   10
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "MANNING",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2404.11794/2404.11794v2.pdf",
  "empreinte": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "page": 11,
  "citation": "all three causes had a statistically significant effect on the probability of a deal.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   11
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "MANNING",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2404.11794/2404.11794v2.pdf",
  "empreinte": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "page": 14,
  "citation": "When we estimated the SCM with interactions, the interaction between the judge’s case count and the defendant’s remorse was nontrivial",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   14
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "MANNING",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2404.11794/2404.11794v2.pdf",
  "empreinte": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "page": 18,
  "citation": "Could an LLM do a “thought experiment” (i.e., make a prediction based on a prompt) about a proposed in silico experiment and achieve the same insight?",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   18
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "MANNING",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2404.11794/2404.11794v2.pdf",
  "empreinte": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "page": 18,
  "citation": "All predictions are made by the LLM once at temperature 0.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   18
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "MANNING",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2404.11794/2404.11794v2.pdf",
  "empreinte": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "page": 19,
  "citation": "In contrast, auction theory is highly accurate in its predictions of the final bid price in the experiment",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   19
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "MANNING",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2404.11794/2404.11794v2.pdf",
  "empreinte": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "page": 19,
  "citation": "In 80/343 simulations, the agents made the maximum number of statements (20) allowed by the system before the auction ended.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   19
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "MANNING",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2404.11794/2404.11794v2.pdf",
  "empreinte": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "page": 19,
  "citation": "We remove these observations because, without additional information, auction theory does not make predictions about partially completed auctions.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   19
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "MANNING",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2404.11794/2404.11794v2.pdf",
  "empreinte": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "page": 21,
  "citation": "We prompted the LLM to predict the path estimates and whether they would be statistically significant for the simulated experiments in Section 3.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   21
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "MANNING",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2404.11794/2404.11794v2.pdf",
  "empreinte": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "page": 22,
  "citation": "That improvement is feasible with the system: there exists an SCM perfectly consistent with auction theory.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   22
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "MANNING",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2404.11794/2404.11794v2.pdf",
  "empreinte": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "page": 22,
  "citation": "If allowed to generate and test enough potential causes, our system could have selected this variable as a possible cause by itself.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   22
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "MANNING",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2404.11794/2404.11794v2.pdf",
  "empreinte": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "page": 22,
  "citation": "It is also less accurate than the mechanical predictions made by the fitted SCM using the same procedure",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   22
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "MANNING",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2404.11794/2404.11794v2.pdf",
  "empreinte": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "page": 22,
  "citation": "When we do fit this SCM (see Figure A.9), the coefficient is close to one",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   22
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "MANNING",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2404.11794/2404.11794v2.pdf",
  "empreinte": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "page": 24,
  "citation": "Statistically significant paths are marked in red (α = 0.05).",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   24
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "MANNING",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2404.11794/2404.11794v2.pdf",
  "empreinte": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "page": 27,
  "citation": "We also showed that such simulations produce results that are highly consistent with theoretical predictions made by the relevant economic theory.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "c44f50f3fb217788fe19523e77e0818247405e581531c5ad4956037b7e2f6192",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   27
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "MANNING",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2404.11794/2404.11794v2.pdf",
